# AGENTS.md

This project uses **xera** for AI-driven QA testing: AI coding-agent skills
generate, run, and diagnose Playwright/HTTP tests from issue-tracker tickets.
This file orients any AI agent (Claude Code, Cursor, OpenAI Codex CLI).

## Skills (how you drive xera)

- `/xera-run <TICKET>` — full pipeline: fetch → feature → script → exec → report
- `/xera-fetch <TICKET>` — pull the ticket into `.xera/<TICKET>/story.md`
- `/xera-feature <TICKET>` — generate the Gherkin `test.feature`
- `/xera-script <TICKET>` — generate the runnable spec
- `/xera-exec <TICKET>` / `/xera-report <TICKET>` — run tests + classify failures
- `/xera-coverage`, `/xera-impact`, `/xera-promote` — coverage, blast-radius, PR promotion
{{#if isReuseWebSession}}- `/xera-http-auth-discover <role>` — one-shot AI discovery of cookies for
  `reuse-web-session` strategy. Drives the Edit tool to apply the proposed
  `reuseWebSession: { ... }` block to `xera.config.ts`. Runs once after the
  web auth-setup; do NOT auto-trigger from `/xera-run`.
{{/if}}

## Scripts (deterministic plumbing the skills call)

You rarely run these directly. The skills do. But if you need to:

| Command | When to run |
|---|---|
| `npx xera-internal fetch <TICKET>` | Pull ticket into `.xera/<TICKET>/` |
| `npx xera-internal exec <TICKET>` | Run Playwright/HTTP tests (add `--reporter=html` for HTML report) |
| `npx xera-internal report <TICKET> --input=<normalized.json>` | Classify failures + write report |
| `npx xera doctor` | Health check (config schema, prompts, auth files) |
| `npx xera doctor --strict` | Stricter gating (used by `/xera-run` Step 0) |
| `npx xera dashboard` | Cross-ticket dashboard (text/JSON/HTML) of latest test results |
| `npx xera dashboard --serve` | Interactive HTML viewer at 127.0.0.1:9323 with click-through to per-ticket reports |
{{#if wantsWeb}}| `XERA_HEADED=1 npx xera-internal auth-setup --role <role> --shape web` | Capture web SSO session (1×, headed for MFA) |
{{/if}}{{#if wantsHttp}}| `npx xera-internal auth-setup --role <role> --shape http` | Produce HTTP auth file from config |
{{#if isReuseWebSession}}| `npx xera-internal verify-http-auth --role <role> --path /api/health` | Smoke test: real GET against API, surface 401/403 with hints |
| `npx xera-internal stage-auth --role <role>` | Decrypt auth state to `.xera/.auth/.cache/` for debugging |
{{/if}}{{/if}}

{{#if isReuseWebSession}}## HTTP auth: reuse-web-session lifecycle

This project's HTTP API rides the web app's SSO session (shared parent-domain cookies). Important cycle:

1. **One-shot setup** (do once per project):
   - `XERA_HEADED=1 npx xera-internal auth-setup --role <role> --shape web` — login, navigate through ≥1 page that calls the API (this sets the CSRF cookie), close browser.
   - `/xera-http-auth-discover <role>` — AI proposes cookie names. The skill Edits `xera.config.ts` for you; review the diff before accepting.
   - `npx xera-internal auth-setup --role <role> --shape http` — derive the HTTP auth file from the web one.

2. **Refresh cycle** (recurring):
   - **Every ~15 minutes** (access cookie TTL): `npx xera-internal auth-setup --role <role> --shape http`. No web re-login needed.
   - **Every ~8 hours** (SSO session TTL): `XERA_HEADED=1 npx xera-internal auth-setup --role <role> --shape web`, THEN re-derive http. `xera.config.ts` is unchanged.
   - Doctor warns 30 minutes before web expiry.

3. **Debugging surface errors**:
   - `doctor` reports `CSRF cookie 'X' not present` → re-run web auth-setup, click through an API-calling page before closing.
   - `doctor` reports `cookies persisted: false` → the preset matchers didn't hit anything; tighten them via `/xera-http-auth-discover` re-run or hand-edit.
   - POST returns 403 but GET works → CSRF header name mismatch. Open DevTools on the web app, inspect a POST request's `X-*` headers, fix `csrf.header` in `xera.config.ts`.

NEVER hand-edit `.xera/.auth/*.json` (encrypted) or generated artifacts under `.xera/<TICKET>/`. Always go through `auth-setup` and skills.
{{/if}}

## Project conventions

{{#if wantsWeb}}- Web UI tests via Playwright (`@xera-ai/web`).
{{/if}}{{#if wantsHttp}}- HTTP API tests (`@xera-ai/http`), OpenAPI-aware when `http.spec` is set.
{{/if}}- Generated artifacts live under `.xera/<TICKET>/` — do not hand-edit; re-run the skill.
- Configuration is in `xera.config.ts`. Secrets go in `.env` (never commit it).
- Auth state lives under `.xera/.auth/` — AES-256-GCM encrypted, gitignored. Use `stage-auth` to inspect.
- Run `npx @xera-ai/cli doctor` if anything looks misconfigured.

